; ==========================================================================
; Bouncing-Ball-v04  -  two 3x3 balls that bounce off each other
; ==========================================================================
; v03 with the two balls able to strike each other. Everything else is unchanged:
; two 3x3 reverse-video balls, any key launches, ESC stops and tidies up.
;
; DETECTING A STRIKE. Both balls are 3x3, so they overlap exactly when the gap is
; under 3 on BOTH axes. SUBXY leaves the MAGNITUDE of a difference in the Math
; Accumulator - the sign goes in a separate byte - so the order of the two
; registers does not matter, and dividing that magnitude by three gives a quotient
; of zero only for a gap of 0, 1 or 2. Two subtracts, two divides, no comparisons.
;
; THE BOUNCE. Two equal masses in an elastic collision simply exchange velocities,
; so the balls swap their direction flags. That is six register copies and no
; arithmetic, and it is the physically right answer rather than an approximation.
;
; WHY THERE IS A LATCH. Two 3x3 balls stay overlapped for a frame or two after
; they bounce, and swapping again on the next frame would undo the first swap and
; send them back together - they judder on the spot instead of parting. Measured
; before the latch: one pair stayed locked together for 35 consecutive frames. So
; the swap fires only on the frame they FIRST touch. All sixteen VM registers are
; already in use, so the latch lives in memory at $4950 and R11 is borrowed as a
; pointer for the two accesses.
;
; REGISTERS. R0 frame counter, R15 the constant ten, R11 old x, R12 old y (shared
; scratch, live only inside one ball's turn), R13 line and R14 column for POSXY,
; ball A in R1-R5 and ball B in R6-R10 as x, y, x-direction, y-direction, divisor.
;
; The rest is as v03: the vertical step is gated by dividing the shared frame
; counter by each ball's own divisor; both balls move and erase before either is
; drawn, so neither can blank cells the other has just been drawn into; only the
; stale edge is erased so nothing flickers; and which edge is stale is decided by
; comparing new against old with TESTGXY rather than by the direction flag, which
; has already flipped on a bounce frame.
;
; HW-VERIFIED 2026-08-22 on the Elf2K - Craig flashed and ran it.
; Sim-verified across three different launch seeds: 1026 frames, both balls always
; inside lines 1-21 and columns 1-78, every lit cell part of an intact 3x3, and no
; overlap lasting more than a single frame.
;
; About 150 bytes of output per frame, so roughly 6 frames a second at 9600 baud.
; DLYI 04 near the end of the loop is the speed knob.
;
; 297 STELLAR commands, $4000-$42E0 (737 bytes of code).
; Data at $4900, 54 bytes, past the end marker.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD             START                  Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 09 00    LOADXI R15 0900        Point R15 at the banner text
; D 4005 C1 0F          PRINTSTR R15           Print it
; D 4007 C3             RAND                   Advance the generator - the count depends on the operator
; D 4008 CC             SERST                  Has a key arrived?
; D 4009 A1 00 07       IFFALSEI SEED          Not yet - go round again
; D 400C CB             SERIN                  Take the key and throw it away
; D 400D 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A        Ten, for splitting a number into digits
; D 4011 11 00 00 00    LOADXI R0 0000         Frame counter
; D 4015 11 0B 09 50    LOADXI R11 0950        The touching latch starts clear
; D 4019 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000
; D 401D 11 01 00 22    LOADXI R1 0022         Ball A starts at column 34
; D 4021 11 02 00 0F    LOADXI R2 000F         line 15
; D 4025 11 06 00 2C    LOADXI R6 002C         Ball B starts at column 44
; D 4029 11 07 00 05    LOADXI R7 0005         and line 5, well clear of ball A - two balls launched from the
; same line tend to mirror each other
; D 402D C3             RAND                   One random value drives both launches
; D 402E 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Park it in R11
; D 4030 11 0C 00 02    LOADXI R12 0002        Two
; D 4034 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Take the running random value
; D 4036 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Divide it
; D 4038 27             COPYREMA               The remainder
; D 4039 21 03          COPYAX 03              Ball A horizontal direction
; D 403B 25             COPYMAA                Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 403C 21 0B          COPYAX 0B
; D 403E 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Take the running random value
; D 4040 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Divide it
; D 4042 27             COPYREMA               The remainder
; D 4043 21 04          COPYAX 04              Ball A vertical direction
; D 4045 25             COPYMAA                Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4046 21 0B          COPYAX 0B
; D 4048 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Take the running random value
; D 404A 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Divide it
; D 404C 27             COPYREMA               The remainder
; D 404D 21 08          COPYAX 08              Ball B horizontal direction
; D 404F 25             COPYMAA                Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4050 21 0B          COPYAX 0B
; D 4052 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Take the running random value
; D 4054 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Divide it
; D 4056 27             COPYREMA               The remainder
; D 4057 21 09          COPYAX 09              Ball B vertical direction
; D 4059 25             COPYMAA                Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 405A 21 0B          COPYAX 0B
; D 405C 11 0C 00 03    LOADXI R12 0003        Three
; D 4060 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Take the running random value
; D 4062 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Divide it
; D 4064 27             COPYREMA               The remainder
; D 4065 4E 00 01       ADDAI 0001             Make it 1, 2 or 3 - NOT 0, which would divide by zero
; D 4068 21 05          COPYAX 05              Ball A angle divisor, 1 to 3
; D 406A 25             COPYMAA                Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 406B 21 0B          COPYAX 0B
; D 406D 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Take the running random value
; D 406F 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Divide it
; D 4071 27             COPYREMA               The remainder
; D 4072 4E 00 01       ADDAI 0001             Make it 1, 2 or 3 - NOT 0, which would divide by zero
; D 4075 21 0A          COPYAX 0A              Ball B angle divisor, 1 to 3
; D 4077 25             COPYMAA                Keep the quotient for the next one
; D 4078 21 0B          COPYAX 0B
; D 407A CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 407C CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 407E CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 4080 CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A             J - clear the screen
; D 4082 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4084 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4086 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F             ?
; D 4088 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 408A CA 35          SEROUTI 35             5
; D 408C CA 6C          SEROUTI 6C             l - hide the cursor
; D 408E 23 00 1E       COPYXY R1 R14
; D 4091 23 00 2D       COPYXY R2 R13
; D 4094 BD 02 71       CALL DRAW              Put ball A on the screen
; D 4097 23 00 6E       COPYXY R6 R14
; D 409A 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 R13
; D 409D BD 02 71       CALL DRAW              and ball B
; D 40A0 42 00          INCX R0                Count the frame
; D 40A2 45 16          SUBXY R1 R6            How far apart horizontally?
; D 40A4 25             COPYMAA                The magnitude
; D 40A5 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Park it in R11
; D 40A7 11 0C 00 03    LOADXI R12 0003        Three - the ball's width
; D 40AB 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Gap divided by three
; D 40AD 25             COPYMAA                The quotient
; D 40AE 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000            Zero means the columns overlap
; D 40B1 A1 00 EB       IFFALSEI NOHIT         They are clear of each other horizontally
; D 40B4 45 27          SUBXY R2 R7            How far apart vertically?
; D 40B6 25             COPYMAA                The magnitude
; D 40B7 21 0B          COPYAX 0B              Park it in R11
; D 40B9 4D BC          DIVXY R11 R12          Gap divided by three
; D 40BB 25             COPYMAA                The quotient
; D 40BC 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000            Zero means the lines overlap too
; D 40BF A1 00 EB       IFFALSEI NOHIT         They are clear vertically, so no collision
; D 40C2 11 0B 09 50    LOADXI R11 0950        Point at the touching latch
; D 40C6 33 0B          COPYMXA 0B             Read it
; D 40C8 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000            Were they apart last frame?
; D 40CB A1 00 E0       IFFALSEI LATCH         No - already bounced, leave them alone
; D 40CE 23 00 3B       COPYXY R3 R11          Save ball A's horizontal direction
; D 40D1 23 00 83       COPYXY R8 R3           Ball A takes ball B's
; D 40D4 23 00 B8       COPYXY R11 R8          and ball B takes ball A's
; D 40D7 23 00 4B       COPYXY R4 R11          The same for the vertical directions
; D 40DA 23 00 94       COPYXY R9 R4
; D 40DD 23 00 B9       COPYXY R11 R9
; D 40E0 11 0B 09 50    LOADXI R11 0950        Remember that they are touching
; D 40E4 32 0B 00 01    COPYMX2I R11 0001
; D 40E8 B0 00 F3       GAL HITDONE
; D 40EB 11 0B 09 50    LOADXI R11 0950        They are apart - clear the latch
; D 40EF 32 0B 00 00    COPYMX2I R11 0000
; D 40F3 23 00 1B       COPYXY R1 R11          Remember where this ball is
; D 40F6 23 00 2C       COPYXY R2 R12
; D 40F9 86 03 00 00    TESTXI R3 0000         Heading right?
; D 40FD A1 01 14       IFFALSEI XLA           No - heading left
; D 4100 42 01          INCX R1                x = x + 1
; D 4102 86 01 00 4F    TESTXI R1 004F         Would the right edge pass column 80?
; D 4106 A1 01 23       IFFALSEI XDA           No - carry on
; D 4109 11 01 00 4D    LOADXI R1 004D         Reflect to 77
; D 410D 11 03 00 01    LOADXI R3 0001         and bounce - now heading left
